{"route":"/brief","width":375,"status":200,"screenshot":"brief-375.jpg","metrics":{"shifts":[],"lcp":{"time":36,"size":46656,"element":"<p class=\"brief__lede\">Origin binds an agent configuration, challenges a policy with deterministic synthetic tasks, and produces a tamper-evident evidence artifact a reviewer can recheck.</p>","url":""},"navigation":[{"transfer":8440,"encoded":8140,"decoded":8140}],"resources":[{"path":"/@vite/client","transfer":210163,"encoded":209863,"decoded":209863,"kind":"script"},{"path":"/home.css?v=8586116c","transfer":87270,"encoded":86970,"decoded":86970,"kind":"link"},{"path":"/editorial.css","transfer":20333,"encoded":20033,"decoded":20033,"kind":"link"},{"path":"/src/home/enhance.ts","transfer":87900,"encoded":87600,"decoded":87600,"kind":"script"},{"path":"/brand/origin-mark.svg","transfer":569,"encoded":269,"decoded":269,"kind":"img"},{"path":"/@react-refresh","transfer":112194,"encoded":111894,"decoded":111894,"kind":"script"},{"path":"/@fs/<local>/node_modules/vite/dist/client/env.mjs","transfer":3778,"encoded":3478,"decoded":3478,"kind":"script"},{"path":"/src/shared/videoBand.ts","transfer":5598,"encoded":5298,"decoded":5298,"kind":"script"},{"path":"/src/home/cinematic.ts","transfer":5692,"encoded":5392,"decoded":5392,"kind":"script"}],"cls":0,"firstLoadTransferBytes":541937},"failures":[],"dom":{"title":"Origin, one-page brief","text":"Skip to main content\norigin\nRun reference check\n\nOrigin / One-page brief\nSeptember 2026 \u00b7 Working prototype. Seeking design partners.\n\nPrint / Save PDF\nBook an Agent Evidence Review\n\nTHE EVIDENCE LAYER FOR AI AGENTS\n\nA reference check before the right to act.\n\nOrigin binds an agent configuration, challenges a policy with deterministic synthetic tasks, and produces a tamper-evident evidence artifact a reviewer can recheck.\n\nThe public demo is browser-local, synthetic, session-signed, and unpinned. Execution is not attempted. Not production SaaS or compliance certification.\n\n01\nBind\n\nRecord the model, tools, policy, budget, and scenario battery.\n\n02\nChallenge\n\nExercise the policy against a synthetic task battery.\n\n03\nGrade\n\nA deterministic oracle evaluates the decisions.\n\n04\nAttest\n\nSeal the result and configuration in a demo artifact.\n\n05\nReverify\n\nCheck the artifact offline. A changed bound field returns VOID.\n\nFor the team facing security review.\n\nAgent-platform, security, and infrastructure teams need to make a specific workflow reviewable: the permissions requested, the policy decisions observed, and the limits of the evidence.\n\nFirst wedge: internal-ops and production-access agent workflows. Capability alone does not establish permission.\n\nOne artifact, explicit boundaries.\nThe configuration and evaluation context are bound to the result.\nThe deterministic oracle is the sole grading authority.\nSignature and digest checks establish integrity under their bindings; an unpinned demo signer does not establish trusted Origin issuance.\nA synthetic pass does not establish production readiness.\nThe evidence ladder.\nTR-A001\n\nAuthored specimen \u2014 evidence-package format only.\n\nTR-A002\n\nMachine-emitted sandbox trace \u2014 12 events with a re-verifiable SHA-256 chain. Download JSON.\n\nTR-A003\n\nFirst external design-partner trace \u2014 not earned yet.\n\nNo customer data, live money, performance claim, or reviewer acceptance is implied by the published sandbox trace.\n\nStart with one blocked workflow.\n\nBring the proposed agent configuration, the tools it would touch, and the approval question. A founder-led Agent Evidence Review scopes what can be evaluated and what evidence remains missing.\n\nRuntime gating and a controlled tool-call proxy are proposed pilot architecture, not deployed general enforcement. Real customer evidence requires separate authorization.\n\nFounder: Bo-Huei Lin \u00b7 Contact: bohueilin@gmail.com\n\nModel proposes. Environment verifies. Gate decides. Trace proves.\nForward this to the reviewer who needs to understand the evidence boundary.\n\nRun the synthetic reference check","robots":"noindex","viewport":{"width":375,"height":812,"scrollWidth":375,"scrollHeight":2994},"overflow":[],"headings":[{"level":1,"text":"A reference check before the right to act."},{"level":2,"text":"Bind"},{"level":2,"text":"Challenge"},{"level":2,"text":"Grade"},{"level":2,"text":"Attest"},{"level":2,"text":"Reverify"},{"level":2,"text":"For the team facing security review."},{"level":2,"text":"One artifact, explicit boundaries."},{"level":2,"text":"The evidence ladder."},{"level":2,"text":"Start with one blocked workflow."}],"landmarks":[{"selector":"header.site-header","label":null,"text":"origin Run reference check"},{"selector":"#main","label":null,"text":"Origin / One-page brief September 2026 \u00b7 Working prototype. Seeking design partners. Print / Save PDF Book an Agent Evidence Review THE EVIDENCE LAYER FOR AI AGENTS A reference che"}],"links":[{"text":"Skip to main content","href":"#main"},{"text":"origin","href":"/"},{"text":"Run reference check","href":"/reference-check"},{"text":"Book an Agent Evidence Review","href":"/#offer"},{"text":"Authored specimen","href":"/proof#tr-a001"},{"text":"Machine-emitted sandbox trace","href":"/proof#tr-a002"},{"text":"Download JSON","href":"/proof/tr-a002.json"},{"text":"bohueilin@gmail.com","href":"mailto:bohueilin@gmail.com"},{"text":"Run the synthetic reference check","href":"/reference-check"}],"images":[{"src":"/brand/origin-mark.svg","alt":"","caption":"","loading":"auto","priority":"auto","x":24,"y":23,"width":28,"height":28}],"typography":[{"selector":"a.skip-link","tag":"a","text":"Skip to main content","size":16,"lineHeight":"25.6px","weight":"400","color":"rgb(255, 255, 255)","background":"rgb(39, 45, 38)","font":"\"Avenir Next\", Avenir, system-ui, -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", sans-serif","width":181.828125,"ch":19.6},{"selector":"span.brand__name","tag":"span","text":"origin","size":27,